Hi,<br>yes, you are right about bullet. But the point is that it's really too complicated. The collision system involves creation of bodies, their form, location, weight, velocities, the size of the world, etc. are considered when collisions are detected. <br>All this involves sophisticated mathematics calculations and lots of RAM.<br>You can look at 2D physics libraries, if you are convinced, that physics is required. That would much increase the performance.<br><br>BR.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=6156">mako90</a> — Fri Feb 05, 2010 8:44 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
